    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math challenging, even though I’ve studied it formally. It feels abstract and disconnected from real life, unlike literature or history which I connect to personally. My parents—especially my mom with her PhD—encouraged me to persevere, but I still see math as a hurdle rather than a passion. I appreciate its structure, but it doesn’t spark the same curiosity as stories or history.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, especially when faced with complex problems or when I feel I’m falling behind. My neuroticism score is high, so anxiety tends to surface in uncertain situations. Math often feels like a maze with no clear path, and when I can’t grasp a concept quickly, it triggers stress. I try to manage it with mindfulness and breaks, especially during exams or problem sets.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI tutor app during my calculus course. It helped me step through problems and offered alternative explanations when I got stuck. It was useful, but I noticed it sometimes gave overly simplified solutions that missed deeper concepts. I found it helpful for checking work, but I still needed to understand the logic myself.",
